<div class="interactive-workflow" data-interactive-tabs aria-label="Interactive Conclave workflow example">
  <div class="tab-nav" role="tablist" aria-label="Workflow stages">
    <button id="tab-btn-discuss" class="tab-btn is-active" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="tab-panel-discuss" tabindex="0" data-tab-target="tab-panel-discuss">
      <strong>1. Discuss</strong>
      <span>People align before execution</span>
    </button>
    <button id="tab-btn-run" class="tab-btn" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tab-panel-run" tabindex="-1" data-tab-target="tab-panel-run">
      <strong>2. Run</strong>
      <span>Start an explicit Work Request</span>
    </button>
    <button id="tab-btn-coordinate" class="tab-btn" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tab-panel-coordinate" tabindex="-1" data-tab-target="tab-panel-coordinate">
      <strong>3. Coordinate</strong>
      <span>Route each step to the right capability</span>
    </button>
    <button id="tab-btn-verify" class="tab-btn" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tab-panel-verify" tabindex="-1" data-tab-target="tab-panel-verify">
      <strong>4. Verify</strong>
      <span>Review changes and evidence</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="tab-content">
    <div id="tab-panel-discuss" class="tab-panel is-active" data-tab-panel="tab-panel-discuss" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-btn-discuss" tabindex="0">
      <div class="run-card__header"><span>Discuss</span><strong>Authentication redesign</strong></div>
      <div class="conversation-preview">
        <p><strong>Alex</strong><span>The refresh flow still has a race condition.</span></p>
        <p><strong>Vitalii</strong><span>Agreed. Fix it and add a regression test.</span></p>
      </div>
      <p>Discussion is side-effect free. Your team can explore ideas and agree on the next step without accidentally starting AI work.</p>
    </div>

    <div id="tab-panel-run" class="tab-panel" data-tab-panel="tab-panel-run" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-btn-run" tabindex="0" hidden>
      <div class="run-card__header"><span>Work Request</span><strong>Fix refresh race and add regression coverage</strong></div>
      <div class="work-request-preview">
        <span>Workflow</span><strong>Implementation → Test → Review</strong>
        <span>Primary Workspace</span><strong>MacBook Pro</strong>
        <button type="button" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">Run</button>
      </div>
      <p>AI execution is explicit. The request, workflow, requester, execution environment, and account policy are known before work starts.</p>
    </div>

    <div id="tab-panel-coordinate" class="tab-panel" data-tab-panel="tab-panel-coordinate" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-btn-coordinate" tabindex="0" hidden>
      <div class="run-card__header"><span>Workflow</span><strong>Best capability for each step</strong></div>
      <div class="coordination-preview">
        <div><span>Research</span><strong>Claude Code</strong></div>
        <div><span>Implementation</span><strong>Codex</strong></div>
        <div><span>Tests</span><strong>Workspace tools</strong></div>
        <div><span>Review</span><strong>Independent model</strong></div>
      </div>
      <p>Workers are selected by role, capability, authorization, availability, and policy instead of binding an entire project to one model.</p>
    </div>

    <div id="tab-panel-verify" class="tab-panel" data-tab-panel="tab-panel-verify" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-btn-verify" tabindex="0" hidden>
      <div class="run-card__header"><span>Result</span><strong>Work Request completed</strong></div>
      <div class="evidence-preview">
        <span>✓ 7 files changed</span>
        <span>✓ Tests passed</span>
        <span>✓ Independent review completed</span>
        <span>✓ Checkpoint recorded</span>
      </div>
      <p>Conclave keeps the result, evidence, findings, and execution history together so the team can inspect what actually happened.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
